{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1785106683,"nonce":"7Au1tDp/ByvoXaOnncZO/VUgcCU=","title":"MED: the published scarab-wsfetch:edge can be older than the fetcher's source — image.yml only watches docker/wsfetch/**","message":"The ADR-0061 fetcher's binary is a bin target of `crates/scarab-workspace-client`\n(deliberately — it reuses the one `Cas::materialize`). But\n`.github/workflows/image.yml`'s path filter watches `docker/wsfetch/**`, not the\ncrate. So a PR that changes the fetcher's Rust and merges to main publishes NO new\n`scarab-wsfetch:edge`, and every consumer of that tag then runs last week's\nfetcher against this week's control plane:\n\n- `deploy/helm/scarab/values.yaml` / `deploy/local-helm` default to the `edge`\n  tag, so the Helm dogfood silently pairs a stale fetcher with a fresh server;\n- `DEFAULT_WSFETCH_IMAGE` in `crates/scarab-executor-k8s/src/lib.rs` is\n  `ghcr.io/thulasi-ram/scarab-wsfetch:edge`, so that is also the PRODUCTION\n  default for anyone who does not override `SCARAB_WSFETCH_IMAGE`.\n\nThis is the workspace-feed path — a fetcher that materialises a snapshot slightly\ndifferently from what the CAS now records is exactly the \"reports success but\nstructurally cannot work\" seam, and version skew there is invisible until a Step\nreads a tree that is subtly wrong.\n\nFiled rather than fixed because `image.yml` was outside the lane of the change\nthat found it (PR #93). `.github/workflows/kind.yml` sidesteps the problem for the\nkind tier by ALWAYS building the fetcher from the tree and never pulling the tag\n— see the \"Build the workspace fetcher image from the tree\" step and the comment\nabove it, which is the argument in miniature.\n\nFix: add `crates/scarab-workspace-client/**` (and `Cargo.lock`) to image.yml's\npath filters, or narrow it to the wsfetch matrix entry.\n\nNote this whole image goes away with the node driver (git-bug 0628369), so the\ncheap filter change is likely the right size of fix.","files":null}]}